# DEFECT 2558, beside it: a null read on the program's own stack is told
# without asking the library before the runtime (2026-11-15).
#
# Asking the earlier handler about every fault was built and measured first,
# and it lost the program's own mistakes: a null read in C on `main`, in a
# program linking a Go archive it had not yet called, died at 139 twice and
# hung once in three runs, both streams empty, since Go's handler on a thread
# it has never seen forwards the fault to the default or waits. A fault on the
# stack the runtime measured for the thread is the program's, and is told at
# once. The library here ends the process in silence when it is handed a fault
# it did not make, as Go does then, so a guard that asked it would leave this
# case with nothing on stderr (`fixedbugs-2558-library.h`).

extern "fixedbugs-2558-library.h"
    function lib_ends_in_silence()
    function lib_read_here() -> i64

function main()
    lib_ends_in_silence()
    print("before")
    print(lib_read_here())
